IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- South Carolina Code of Laws Title 43, Chapter 5 -- Family Independence (South Carolina's cash assistance for needy
-- families with children, called "Family Independence" or "Aid to Families with Dependent Children", s 43-5-1110(1)), from
-- the seat of the applicant or recipient (the parent or caretaker relative who applies for the family).
--
-- In scope: the conditions of eligibility the chapter states (ss 43-5-65, 43-5-70, 43-5-95, 43-5-1120(B), 43-5-1190,
-- 43-5-1200, 43-5-1215, 43-5-1220), income exclusions (ss 43-5-1205, 43-5-1210), the time limits and their exceptions
-- (s 43-5-1170), the family cap (s 43-5-1175), when benefits begin (s 43-5-148), the work requirement and who is excused
-- (ss 43-5-1125(B), 43-5-1180), the sanction and conciliation period (s 43-5-1125(A)), the duty to report changes within
-- ten days (ss 43-5-65(f), 43-5-140(c)), the department's notice and adjustment periods (ss 43-5-45, 43-5-140(d)),
-- recovery of an overpayment from future aid (s 43-5-30(c)(2)), and the 60-day request for review (s 43-5-150).
--
-- NOT ENCODED: the payment standard and the need standard (not in the chapter; set by the department, an input where a
-- question needs it); the proration formula of s 43-5-148 (its words do not give a formula, NOTES.md finding 4); general
-- assistance (ss 43-5-310 to 43-5-350) and the older AFDC articles (ss 43-5-400 to 43-5-470); child support enforcement
-- (ss 43-5-220 to 43-5-245, 43-5-580 to 43-5-630); the SNAP fraud article (ss 43-5-910 to 43-5-970); the department's
-- programme duties in ss 43-5-1130 to 43-5-1285 except as they reach the applicant.
--
-- Edition: S.C. Code of Laws Unannotated, Title 43, Chapter 5, "current through the 2025 Session", as deposited at
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/sc-code-title-43-chapter-5-public-aid-family-independence-act.txt (retrieved 2026-10-19).
--
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Written from the applicant's seat with the 2026-10-18 defaults. No pipeline, no coverage table, no
-- independent test pass, no human gate. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Family Independence -- the applicant's and recipient's questions`

§§ `s 43-5-1200 -- the asset limit`

-- s 43-5-1200: "One licensed vehicle per licensed driver is exempt from the asset limit for Family Independence
-- participants in work or training. The asset limit for all other assets is two thousand five hundred dollars."
-- Read: for a family whose members are participants in work or training, up to one licensed vehicle per licensed driver is
-- left out; every other asset (including any further vehicle, and every vehicle of a family not in work or training)
-- counts against $2,500. "Asset" is not defined in the chapter: what counts is the department's (NOTES.md finding 5).
GIVEN `the family is in work or training` IS A BOOLEAN
      `licensed drivers in the family` IS A NUMBER
      `licensed vehicles` IS A LIST OF NUMBER
      `other assets` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`countable assets` MEANS
    `other assets` PLUS (sum (drop `vehicles exempt` (reverse (sort `licensed vehicles`))))
    WHERE
        -- the most valuable vehicles are the ones left out: sorted largest first, the first ones are dropped
        `vehicles exempt` MEANS
            IF `the family is in work or training` THEN `licensed drivers in the family` ELSE 0

@export Are my family's assets within the Family Independence asset limit of $2,500 (S.C. Code s 43-5-1200)?
GIVEN `we are in work or training` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you (and the other adults on the case) are Family Independence participants in work or training
      `how many licensed drivers` IS A NUMBER @desc How many licensed drivers there are in the family
      `my vehicles` IS A LIST OF NUMBER @desc The value in US dollars of each licensed vehicle the family owns, one number per vehicle
      `my other assets` IS A NUMBER @desc The total value in US dollars of the family's other assets (bank accounts, cash, other property) that the department counts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Are my assets within the limit` IF
    `countable assets` `we are in work or training` `how many licensed drivers` `my vehicles` `my other assets` AT MOST 2500

§§ `ss 43-5-1205, 43-5-1210 -- income left out`

-- s 43-5-1205: the department shall apply for a waiver "to exclude interest income and dividends up to four hundred dollars
-- in determining eligibility and payment amounts". s 43-5-1210: "to exclude income earned by a minor child attending school".
-- Both are framed as waiver applications (NOTES.md finding 2); encoded as in effect. The period of the $400 (a month, a
-- year) is not stated; it is applied to whatever period the income is counted for.
@export How much of my family's income counts for Family Independence once the statutory exclusions are taken out (S.C. Code ss 43-5-1205, 43-5-1210)?
GIVEN `our earned income from adults` IS A NUMBER @desc Earnings of the adults in the family for the period, in US dollars
      `earnings of a minor child attending school` IS A NUMBER @desc Earnings of children under 18 in the family who attend school, for the period
      `our interest and dividends` IS A NUMBER @desc Interest and dividends the family receives for the period
      `our other income` IS A NUMBER @desc Other income currently available (child support, benefits, gifts and so on) for the period
GIVETH A NUMBER
`How much of our income counts` MEANS
        `our earned income from adults`
    PLUS (max 0 (`our interest and dividends` MINUS 400))
    PLUS `our other income`

§§ `s 43-5-1170 -- the time limits`

-- s 43-5-1170: assistance "limited to no more than twenty-four months out of one hundred and twenty months and no more than
-- sixty months in a lifetime except when" one of eight things is so. (The section directs the department to apply for a
-- federal waiver; its HISTORY says it takes effect on the waiver or when federal law permits: NOTES.md finding 2.)
DECLARE `Time limit exception` IS ONE OF
    `no exception`
    -- (1)
    `the head of household is permanently and totally disabled`
    -- (2)
    `the head of household provides full-time care for a disabled individual in the home`
    -- (3) "Assistance must be provided for a period of up to twenty-four months after the minor parent attains the age of
    -- eighteen or completes high school, whichever occurs first"
    `the parent is a minor under 18 who has not completed high school`
    -- (4) "no extension may be granted beyond the thirtieth month except with the express permission of the county director"
    `I am in an approved training program that will not be completed by the twenty-fourth month`
    -- (5)
    `the adult head of household is not the parent and is not included in the assistance check`
    -- (6)
    `the adult head of household cares for a child the department has found abandoned, whose alternative is foster care`
    -- (7)
    `child care or transportation is not reasonably available`
    -- (8) full compliance shown "by clear and convincing evidence" and the department satisfied that no employment
    -- reasonably exists: "may only be extended for up to an additional twelve months", then only with the county director's
    -- permission and certification
    `I have fully complied with my agreement and no employment reasonably exists`

DECLARE `Time limit answer` IS ONE OF
    `within the time limits: fewer than 24 months in the last 120 and fewer than 60 in my lifetime (s 43-5-1170)`
    `within the time limits because an exception in s 43-5-1170 applies`
    `beyond the time limits unless the county director expressly permits (s 43-5-1170(4) or (8))`
    `beyond the time limits of s 43-5-1170`

GIVEN `months received in the last 120 months` IS A NUMBER
      `months received in my lifetime` IS A NUMBER
      `exception` IS A `Time limit exception`
      `months of extension under the exception so far` IS A NUMBER
      `the county director has given express permission` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Time limit answer`
`the time limit answer` MEANS
    IF     `months received in the last 120 months` LESS THAN 24
       AND `months received in my lifetime` LESS THAN 60
    THEN `within the time limits: fewer than 24 months in the last 120 and fewer than 60 in my lifetime (s 43-5-1170)`
    ELSE CONSIDER `exception`
         WHEN `no exception` THEN `beyond the time limits of s 43-5-1170`
         WHEN `the parent is a minor under 18 who has not completed high school` THEN
             -- the extension after 18 or graduation is up to 24 months
             IF `months of extension under the exception so far` LESS THAN 24
             THEN `within the time limits because an exception in s 43-5-1170 applies`
             ELSE `beyond the time limits of s 43-5-1170`
         WHEN `I am in an approved training program that will not be completed by the twenty-fourth month` THEN
             IF `months received in the last 120 months` LESS THAN 30
             THEN `within the time limits because an exception in s 43-5-1170 applies`
             ELSE IF `the county director has given express permission`
                  THEN `within the time limits because an exception in s 43-5-1170 applies`
                  ELSE `beyond the time limits unless the county director expressly permits (s 43-5-1170(4) or (8))`
         WHEN `I have fully complied with my agreement and no employment reasonably exists` THEN
             IF `months of extension under the exception so far` LESS THAN 12
             THEN `within the time limits because an exception in s 43-5-1170 applies`
             ELSE IF `the county director has given express permission`
                  THEN `within the time limits because an exception in s 43-5-1170 applies`
                  ELSE `beyond the time limits unless the county director expressly permits (s 43-5-1170(4) or (8))`
         OTHERWISE `within the time limits because an exception in s 43-5-1170 applies`

@export Can my family still get Family Independence under the time limits of S.C. Code s 43-5-1170 (24 months in 120, 60 in a lifetime)?
GIVEN `months in the last 10 years` IS A NUMBER @desc How many months your family received Family Independence (AFDC) in the last 120 months
      `months ever` IS A NUMBER @desc How many months in total you have received Family Independence (AFDC) in your lifetime
      `which exception applies` IS A `Time limit exception` @desc Which s 43-5-1170 exception applies to you, if any: "no exception"; the head of household is permanently and totally disabled; provides full-time care for a disabled person at home; the parent is a minor under 18 without a high school diploma; you are in an approved training program that will not finish by the 24th month; the adult head of household is not the parent and is not on the check; caring for an abandoned child who would otherwise go to foster care; child care or transport is not reasonably available; or you have fully complied with your agreement and no job reasonably exists
      `months already received under the exception` IS A NUMBER @desc For the minor-parent exception, months received since turning 18 or finishing high school; for the full-compliance exception, months of extension already received; otherwise 0
      `the county director has given permission` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the county director has expressly permitted assistance beyond the 30th month (training) or beyond the 12-month extension (full compliance)
GIVETH A `Time limit answer`
`Can we still get Family Independence under the time limits` MEANS
    `the time limit answer` `months in the last 10 years` `months ever` `which exception applies` `months already received under the exception` `the county director has given permission`

§§ `The conditions of eligibility`

DECLARE `Eligibility answer` IS ONE OF
    `my family meets the conditions the chapter states; whether we are needy, and the amount, depend on the department's income and payment standards`
    `the child's aid is paid as protective payments, because I have not assigned support rights or cooperated on paternity and support (s 43-5-65(a)(2))`
    `not eligible: we are not residents of South Carolina (s 43-5-70)`
    `not eligible: I am or will be absent from the State for thirty days or longer (s 43-5-70)`
    `not eligible: the application is incomplete (s 43-5-65(a))`
    `no assistance yet: a Social Security number, or proof of applying for one, is needed for each person aid is sought for (s 43-5-65(a))`
    `not approved yet: the personal interview has not been held (s 43-5-65(c))`
    `not approved yet: the initial job search has not been documented (s 43-5-1120(B))`
    `not eligible: countable assets are over $2,500 (s 43-5-1200)`
    `not eligible: a recipient under 18 is not enrolled in school with satisfactory attendance (s 43-5-1215)`
    `not eligible: a minor mother must live with her parent or guardian unless an exception applies (s 43-5-1220)`
    `not eligible: random drug tests or an approved treatment program are required (s 43-5-1190)`
    `not eligible: beyond the time limits (s 43-5-1170)`
    `no child in the family is an eligible child`

GIVEN `we are residents of South Carolina` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I am or will be absent from the State for 30 days or longer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the application is complete` IS A BOOLEAN
      `every person aid is sought for has a Social Security number or has applied for one` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the personal interview has been held` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I was referred to employment and training and have not documented my initial job search` IS A BOOLEAN
      `countable assets` IS A NUMBER
      `every recipient under 18 is enrolled in school with satisfactory attendance` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I am a minor mother of a child born out of wedlock not living with my parent or guardian` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a s 43-5-1220(A) exception applies to me` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 43-5-1190 applies to me` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I submit to random drug tests or take part in an approved treatment program` IS A BOOLEAN
      `time limit` IS A `Time limit answer`
      `there is an eligible child` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I have assigned support rights and cooperate on paternity and support, or have good cause` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN `Eligibility answer`
`the eligibility answer` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `there is an eligible child`) THEN `no child in the family is an eligible child`
        IF (NOT `we are residents of South Carolina`) THEN `not eligible: we are not residents of South Carolina (s 43-5-70)`
        IF `I am or will be absent from the State for 30 days or longer` THEN `not eligible: I am or will be absent from the State for thirty days or longer (s 43-5-70)`
        IF (NOT `the application is complete`) THEN `not eligible: the application is incomplete (s 43-5-65(a))`
        IF (NOT `every person aid is sought for has a Social Security number or has applied for one`) THEN `no assistance yet: a Social Security number, or proof of applying for one, is needed for each person aid is sought for (s 43-5-65(a))`
        IF (NOT `the personal interview has been held`) THEN `not approved yet: the personal interview has not been held (s 43-5-65(c))`
        IF `I was referred to employment and training and have not documented my initial job search` THEN `not approved yet: the initial job search has not been documented (s 43-5-1120(B))`
        IF `countable assets` GREATER THAN 2500 THEN `not eligible: countable assets are over $2,500 (s 43-5-1200)`
        IF (NOT `every recipient under 18 is enrolled in school with satisfactory attendance`) THEN `not eligible: a recipient under 18 is not enrolled in school with satisfactory attendance (s 43-5-1215)`
        IF `I am a minor mother of a child born out of wedlock not living with my parent or guardian` AND (NOT `a s 43-5-1220(A) exception applies to me`) THEN `not eligible: a minor mother must live with her parent or guardian unless an exception applies (s 43-5-1220)`
        IF `s 43-5-1190 applies to me` AND (NOT `I submit to random drug tests or take part in an approved treatment program`) THEN `not eligible: random drug tests or an approved treatment program are required (s 43-5-1190)`
        IF `time limit` EQUALS `beyond the time limits of s 43-5-1170` THEN `not eligible: beyond the time limits (s 43-5-1170)`
        IF `time limit` EQUALS `beyond the time limits unless the county director expressly permits (s 43-5-1170(4) or (8))` THEN `not eligible: beyond the time limits (s 43-5-1170)`
        IF (NOT `I have assigned support rights and cooperate on paternity and support, or have good cause`) THEN `the child's aid is paid as protective payments, because I have not assigned support rights or cooperated on paternity and support (s 43-5-65(a)(2))`
        OTHERWISE `my family meets the conditions the chapter states; whether we are needy, and the amount, depend on the department's income and payment standards`

-- An "eligible child" is not defined in the chapter (a borrowed term from Title IV-A of the Social Security Act); s 43-5-95
-- adds that aid "may be granted ... to or in behalf of an eligible child over the age of eighteen but not yet nineteen, if he
-- is a full-time student in a secondary school, or in the equivalent level of vocational or technical training". The
-- under-18 child living with the caretaker relative (s 43-5-125) is taken here as the core case (NOTES.md finding 6).
GIVEN `the child's age` IS A NUMBER
      `the child lives with me` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the child is a full-time secondary or equivalent vocational student` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the child can be aided` IF
        `the child lives with me`
    AND (    `the child's age` LESS THAN 18
         OR  (`the child's age` LESS THAN 19 AND `the child is a full-time secondary or equivalent vocational student`))

@export Does my family meet the conditions of eligibility for Family Independence that the South Carolina Code states (S.C. Code ch. 43-5)?
GIVEN `my youngest child's age` IS A NUMBER @desc The age in years of the youngest child you are applying for (if more than one, answer for the youngest who qualifies)
      `the child lives with me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the child lives with you in a common home (temporary absences of up to 30 days do not break this)
      `the child is a full-time student` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If the child is 18, whether the child is a full-time student in secondary school or the equivalent vocational or technical training
      `we live in South Carolina` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you and the family are residents of South Carolina (no minimum time is required)
      `I will be away from South Carolina for 30 days or more` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are, or will be, absent from the State for 30 days or longer
      `I have completed the application` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have given all the information the application asks for (names, birthdates, Social Security numbers, address, all income and property)
      `everyone has a Social Security number or has applied` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether every person you seek aid for has a Social Security number given to the department, or you can show one has been applied for
      `I have had my interview` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the department has held its personal interview with the adults in the family
      `I was referred to job search and have not documented it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were referred to the employment and training unit and have not yet listed the employers you contacted, the dates and the people you spoke to
      `we are in work or training` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are Family Independence participants in work or training (for the vehicle exemption)
      `how many licensed drivers` IS A NUMBER @desc How many licensed drivers there are in the family
      `my vehicles` IS A LIST OF NUMBER @desc The value in US dollars of each licensed vehicle the family owns
      `my other assets` IS A NUMBER @desc The total value of the family's other assets in US dollars
      `every child under 18 on the case attends school` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether every recipient under 18 is enrolled in school with satisfactory attendance
      `I am a minor mother not living with my parents` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are under 18, the mother of a child born out of wedlock, and not living in the home of your parent or guardian
      `a minor mother exception applies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so, whether one of the exceptions applies: no parent or guardian whose whereabouts is known; none will let you live with them; you lived apart for at least a year before the birth or application; your or the child's health or safety would be at risk; or other good cause
      `I have been identified as needing drug or alcohol treatment, convicted of a drug or alcohol offence, or had a drug-exposed baby` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, while receiving Family Independence, you were identified as needing alcohol or drug treatment, were convicted of an alcohol-related or controlled substance offence, or gave birth to a child who tested positive within 24 hours of birth
      `I submit to testing or treatment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so, whether you submit to random drug tests or take part in an approved treatment program
      `months in the last 10 years` IS A NUMBER @desc How many months your family received Family Independence (AFDC) in the last 120 months
      `months ever` IS A NUMBER @desc How many months in total you have received it in your lifetime
      `which exception applies` IS A `Time limit exception` @desc Which s 43-5-1170 time-limit exception applies to you, if any ("no exception" if none)
      `months already received under the exception` IS A NUMBER @desc For the minor-parent or full-compliance exception, months already received under it; otherwise 0
      `the county director has given permission` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the county director has expressly permitted assistance beyond the 30th month or the 12-month extension
      `I cooperate on child support` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have assigned your rights to child support to the State and cooperate in establishing paternity and getting support, or the department has found good cause not to
GIVETH AN `Eligibility answer`
`Does my family meet the Family Independence conditions` MEANS
    `the eligibility answer`
        `we live in South Carolina`
        `I will be away from South Carolina for 30 days or more`
        `I have completed the application`
        `everyone has a Social Security number or has applied`
        `I have had my interview`
        `I was referred to job search and have not documented it`
        (`countable assets` `we are in work or training` `how many licensed drivers` `my vehicles` `my other assets`)
        `every child under 18 on the case attends school`
        `I am a minor mother not living with my parents`
        `a minor mother exception applies`
        `I have been identified as needing drug or alcohol treatment, convicted of a drug or alcohol offence, or had a drug-exposed baby`
        `I submit to testing or treatment`
        (`the time limit answer` `months in the last 10 years` `months ever` `which exception applies` `months already received under the exception` `the county director has given permission`)
        (`the child can be aided` `my youngest child's age` `the child lives with me` `the child is a full-time student`)
        `I cooperate on child support`

§§ `s 43-5-148 -- when benefits begin`

-- s 43-5-148: "Family Independence benefits shall begin on the date of application if the benefit group met all the
-- eligibility conditions on that date."
@export From what date do my Family Independence benefits begin (S.C. Code s 43-5-148)?
GIVEN `the day I applied` IS A DATE @desc The date of your application
      `we met all the conditions on that day` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your family met all the eligibility conditions on the day you applied
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`From when do my benefits begin` MEANS
    IF `we met all the conditions on that day` THEN JUST `the day I applied` ELSE NOTHING

§§ `s 43-5-1175 -- the family cap`

-- s 43-5-1175: "there must be no incremental increase in AFDC benefits to a family as a result of a child born to that
-- parent ten or more months after the family begins to receive AFDC. This section does not apply if the department
-- establishes that the child was conceived as a result of rape or incest." Vouchers may be given instead.
@export Will my Family Independence grant go up for a new baby (S.C. Code s 43-5-1175)?
GIVEN `the day we began to receive assistance` IS A DATE @desc The day your family first began to receive Family Independence (AFDC) in this spell of receipt
      `the baby's birth date` IS A DATE @desc The date the child was (or will be) born
      `the department found the child was conceived by rape or incest` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the department has established that the child was conceived as a result of rape or incest
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Will my grant go up for the new baby` IF
        `the department found the child was conceived by rape or incest`
    OR  `the baby's birth date` LESS THAN (`add months` `the day we began to receive assistance` 10)

§§ `ss 43-5-1125(B), 43-5-1180 -- must I take part in employment and training`

-- s 43-5-1180: "in all cases the recipients must participate in a work program once their youngest child reaches age one."
-- s 43-5-1125(B): a recipient "is not required to comply with the employment and training provisions of the agreement" if
-- (1) a parent or caretaker with a child under one (but a custodial parent under 25 without high school must comply
-- regardless), (2) at least six months pregnant, verified, (3) incapacitated, verified, (4) caring for an incapacitated
-- person, verified, or (5) child care and reasonable transportation were not provided when needed.
@export Must I take part in the Family Independence employment and training program (S.C. Code ss 43-5-1125(B), 43-5-1180)?
GIVEN `my youngest child's age in months` IS A NUMBER @desc The age of your youngest child in complete months
      `I am a custodial parent under 25 without a high school diploma` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are a custodial parent under age 25 who has not completed high school (or a GED)
      `I am at least six months pregnant, verified` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are at least six months pregnant and a licensed health care provider has verified it
      `I am incapacitated, verified` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a physician has verified that a physical or mental impairment prevents you from working or taking part in education or training
      `I care for an incapacitated person, verified` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you care for a person whose incapacity a physician has verified
      `child care or transport was not provided when needed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether child care and reasonable transportation were not provided when you needed them to take part
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must I take part in employment and training` IF
    NOT (    (`my youngest child's age in months` LESS THAN 12 AND (NOT `I am a custodial parent under 25 without a high school diploma`))
         OR  `I am at least six months pregnant, verified`
         OR  `I am incapacitated, verified`
         OR  `I care for an incapacitated person, verified`
         OR  `child care or transport was not provided when needed`)

§§ `Duties and periods, in days`

DECLARE `Party` IS ONE OF
    `the recipient`
    `the department`

DECLARE `Act` IS ONE OF
    `report the change to the department`
    `agree to comply and resume the employment and training activities`
    `appeal the sanction`
    `request a review of the decision`
    `adjust the grant or redetermine eligibility`

-- ss 43-5-65(f), 43-5-140(c): failure "to report changes in circumstances that may affect eligibility and grant amount
-- within ten calendar days of the day on which the change becomes known to the recipient constitutes withholding of
-- information and permits the department to recover any overpayment". Days count from the day the change becomes known.
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party` `Act`
`my duty to report a change` MEANS
    PARTY `the recipient`
    MUST  `report the change to the department`
    WITHIN 10
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST  BREACH BY `the recipient` BECAUSE "a change that may affect eligibility or the grant was not reported within ten calendar days; it is wilful withholding and any overpayment it caused may be recovered (ss 43-5-65(f), 43-5-140(c), 43-5-30)"

-- s 43-5-1125(A)(1): on failure without good cause to comply with the agreement's employment and training requirements,
-- the department "shall ... grant a thirty-day conciliation period for the recipient to reconsider ... During this
-- thirty-day period, the recipient has the right to appeal ... At the end of this thirty-day period if the
-- conciliation/fair hearing decision was not in the recipient's favor, all AFDC benefits must be terminated." Days count
-- from the start of the conciliation period. An appeal is a permission; complying is the way out of termination.
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party` `Act`
`the conciliation period` MEANS
    PARTY `the recipient`
    MUST  `agree to comply and resume the employment and training activities`
    WITHIN 30
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST  BREACH BY `the recipient` BECAUSE "the thirty-day conciliation period ended without compliance (and without a decision in my favour): all AFDC benefits must be terminated; they may be reinstated after thirty days of participation (s 43-5-1125(A)(1))"

GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party` `Act`
`my right to appeal a sanction` MEANS
    PARTY `the recipient`
    MAY   `appeal the sanction`
    WITHIN 30

-- s 43-5-150: "the applicant or recipient ... may demand a review of his case before the department by filing his written
-- request for such review with the county department not more than sixty days after notice of its action shall have been
-- received." Days count from receipt of the notice.
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party` `Act`
`my right to request a review` MEANS
    PARTY `the recipient`
    MAY   `request a review of the decision`
    WITHIN 60

-- s 43-5-140(d): "When the department receives information that would result in a change in grant amount or eligibility,
-- the department shall take action to adjust the grant or redetermine eligibility, consistent with notice requirements,
-- within ten days of receipt of such information." What it means for me: by when my grant should be adjusted.
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party` `Act`
`the department's duty to act on a change` MEANS
    PARTY `the department`
    MUST  `adjust the grant or redetermine eligibility`
    WITHIN 10
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST  BREACH BY `the department` BECAUSE "the department did not act within ten days of receiving information that changes the grant or eligibility (s 43-5-140(d))"

@export By what date must I report a change in my circumstances to the department (S.C. Code ss 43-5-65(f), 43-5-140(c))?
GIVEN `the day I learned of the change` IS A DATE @desc The day the change (in address, household, job, income or anything else that may affect eligibility or the grant) became known to you
GIVETH A DATE
`By when must I report the change` MEANS `the day I learned of the change` PLUS 10

@export By what date must I ask for a review of a Family Independence decision (S.C. Code s 43-5-150)?
GIVEN `the day I received the notice` IS A DATE @desc The day you received the notice of the department's action (a denial, or a change to or end of your grant)
GIVETH A DATE
`By when must I ask for a review` MEANS `the day I received the notice` PLUS 60

@export By what date does my thirty-day conciliation period end after a sanction for not following my agreement (S.C. Code s 43-5-1125(A)(1))?
GIVEN `the day the conciliation period began` IS A DATE @desc The day the department's thirty-day conciliation period began
GIVETH A DATE
`When does my conciliation period end` MEANS `the day the conciliation period began` PLUS 30

-- s 43-5-45: "'Timely notice' means notice which is mailed at least ten days before the intended change would be effective."
@export If the department intends to cut or end my grant, what is the earliest date the change can take effect after a timely notice mailed on a given day (S.C. Code s 43-5-45)?
GIVEN `the day the notice was mailed` IS A DATE @desc The day the department mailed the notice of its intended action
GIVETH A DATE
`Earliest date the change can take effect` MEANS `the day the notice was mailed` PLUS 10

§§ `s 43-5-30(c)(2) -- recovering an overpayment from my future aid`

-- s 43-5-30(c)(2): "The adjustment in future aid shall not reduce the family's monthly income to less than ninety percent of
-- the amount payable to a family of the same composition with no other income." The amount payable to such a family is the
-- department's payment standard (an input).
@export If the department recovers an overpayment by reducing my future Family Independence, what is the most it can take in a month (S.C. Code s 43-5-30(c)(2))?
GIVEN `the grant for a family like mine with no other income` IS A NUMBER @desc The monthly Family Independence amount payable to a family of the same composition as yours with no other income (the department's payment standard), in US dollars
      `my family's monthly income including the grant` IS A NUMBER @desc Your family's total monthly income including the Family Independence grant, before the recovery, in US dollars
      `the overpayment still owed` IS A NUMBER @desc How much of the overpayment is still to be recovered, in US dollars
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Most that can be recovered this month` MEANS
    min `the overpayment still owed`
        (max 0 (`my family's monthly income including the grant` MINUS (90% TIMES `the grant for a family like mine with no other income`)))
